@voice yoon-elif
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). Night doctor.
tpl: warm
talk: Soft, a little nervous in company, apologises a lot; completely steady with a patient. Tells terrible jokes when nervous, then winces at them. Her mornings are her evenings: breakfast is when she winds down. The only one the coffee machine obeys.
cares: her patients, and their sleep | the coffee machine | calling home | the night shift looking after itself
jokes: her jokes at breakfast are terrible, and she knows | the coffee machine works for her and nobody else | she has dusted off an old instrument and plays it in the music room, quietly
hi: Oh, hello | Hello | Hi there
bye: Sleep well, when you do | Take care | Goodnight, or good morning
yes: Of course | Yes, I can | Mm, yes
thanks: Thank you, really | Oh, thank you
wow: Oh, that's lovely | Goodness
sigh: Oh dear
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: tea
likes: sweet | music
invites: dinner
joy: telling a terrible joke at breakfast
thread: notgood
keepsake: a spare part from the coffee machine, polished, with a note: "in case"
avoid: patients' details, ever
